 I'm pretty certain I'll find a workaround that fits more with Next's design and concepts.\r\n\r\nSo thanks for helping and good luck down the road. ","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/2067561703/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor":{"login":"bonrow","id":47287352,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjQ3Mjg3MzUy","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/47287352?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow","html_url":"https://github.com/bonrow","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/bonrow/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false}},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/2070757590","html_url":"https://github.com/vercel/next.js/issues/64708#issuecomment-2070757590","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/64708","id":2070757590,"node_id":"IC_kwDOBC3Cis57bUDW","user":{"login":"frankievx","id":12982201,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjEyOTgyMjAx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/12982201?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx","html_url":"https://github.com/frankievx","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/frankievx/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-04-22T19:28:05Z","updated_at":"2024-04-22T19:28:05Z","body":"> Hey Tanner,\r\n> \r\n> I have a dashboard with three different parallel routes being displayed side by side. Some containing route params up to two directories deep. For some slots I need a default.js on different levels, to be able to use the supplied route parameters. I reckon I'm going to have to use normal pages, but the issue is they refetch on some soft navigation changes and also I'll kinda have to spam them in multiple places to get the desired behaviour, which is something I don't particularly want. I'm pretty certain I'll find a workaround that fits more with Next's design and concepts.\r\n> \r\n> So thanks for helping and good luck down the road.\r\n\r\nI'm also interested in this functionality and the ability to have deeply nested slots that run code. My use case is essentially when I'm working on React Three Fiber projects I like to have the canvas and the webgl layer as a slot and then html on the main routes. This separation allows me to organize my react three fiber code effectively and in parallel with the html code.","author_association":"NONE","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/vercel/next.js/issues/comments/2070757590/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"event":"commented","actor"